                <pb facs="0362" n="263" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg263"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">632.6231/61: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-06-02T15:00:00-03:00">June 2, 1936—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 2—2:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>141. Department’s 80 June 1, 7 p.m. I saw Macedo this morning, read to him the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> and at his request left with him a
                    copy. He is to see the President on the subject this afternoon.</p>
                <p>I expect to see the Minister of Finance later in the day.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
